7. Considering the submissions of the learned counsel for the parties and the fact that the role of the petitioner is stated to be general in nature, no specific allegations of entrustment have been made against the petitioner in the FIR; the petitioner is in custody for the last 03 months and 16 days;
though the challan has been presented, the trial of the case is yet to commence; therefore,
continuous detention of the petitioner would not serve the ends of justice.
